    "name": {
      "@id": "foaf:name"
    },
    "_comment_mapping": "Where a BOP concept has an AOP-ontology counterpart it reuses that term, because the two frameworks share a grammar and should be queryable together. The event/relationship structure maps onto aopo directly; no term is minted for the beneficial direction, which is carried by the PATO action on the event instead.",
    "events": {
